    "correction": "syncControl detects native boolean mismatch before Switch.SetChecked and includes it in the existing Update predicate. This repairs the style without invoking Change.",
    "negative_proof": "The unchanged final regression compiled and actually failed against the preserved pre-fix14 source at the selected-background versus accepted-nil assertion. Earlier invalid-manual-config and nil-background-reader failures remain historical fixture failures, not defect proof."
  },
  "source_conclusions": [
    "Four additive public leaf kinds are validated; progress rejects nonfinite/out-of-range Number and passive Change/Activate, Orientation is restricted to progress/separator and horizontal/vertical/empty, and passive kinds stay out of managed focus order.",
    "Switch/ToggleButton use existing bounded PostWindow delivery, latest callback and captured native boolean value, disabled ancestry and retired-record guards, and retained Core Switch identity. The restored native boolean mismatch now guarantees required update/style work.",
    "Core Meter is passive, bounded to the accepted0..1 values; progress and separator orientation stylers follow current descriptor state. Their final managed style hook runs after native dimensional/growth defaults so explicit override and removal restoration remain coherent.",
    "Separator is omitted from accessibility publication; progress has numeric Value and0/1 Min/Max with no focus/actions. Switch/ToggleButton publish boolean Value and only supported focus/press/set handlers. Cocoa role and NSNumber conversion reuse the checkable predicate.",
    "Existing owner generation/lifetime guards continue to protect AX delivery; the new code adds no native read to queued owner callback delivery.",
    "Portable and direct retained tests cover validation, focus, restoration, latest callbacks, disabled/removal refusal, passive semantics, identity and style override/restoration. The rejection fixture exercises actual Core Switch Click/listener/Styler and queued owner Drain/reconcile, with an explicit faithful post-event restyle.",
    "The separate actual Manual fixture routes public key and measured pointer input, captures completed software frames and checks progress-region pixels; its scope remains distinct from physical OS input.",
    "The public catalog and specs describe the controlled/passive limits, independent boolean semantics, and outstanding physical Mac accessibility/input/memory/performance gates."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "This is an internal source review; reviewer executed only bounded file reading/hash/JSON checks, no Go/test/native/UI/provider/settings/Git actions.",
    "Root-owned final targeted/full race, vet, builds and any provider review are separate pending qualification records and are not certified as PASS here.",
    "The rejected-style fixture directly sends a Core Switch event and explicitly runs its post-event styler; it does not itself traverse the complete public Manual router or OS input path. That router is exercised by the separate accepted-change Manual fixture.",
    "Software RGBA evidence and inert Objective-C role/value fixtures do not establish physical display, human VoiceOver, native memory, sustained performance or full Mac acceptance.",
